# Code Structure & API

- Separate UI, state, domain, data access, integrations, utils, config, tests; respect existing layout and dependency direction.
- Prefer web standards, semantic HTML, CSS Grid/Flexbox; avoid unjustified framework lock-in.
- Success envelope (if no project standard): `{ "data", "meta?" }`.
- Errors: prefer RFC 9457 Problem Details; never leak stacks/SQL/secrets to clients.
- HTTP: 200/201/204 success; 400 validation; 401/403 authz; 404; 409; 429; 500/503.
- Load only what the first view needs; optimize from measurements.

